maluos-gateway (0.4.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13, shared GPUs, slice G2 (docs/inference-node-api.md, surface 1;
    docs/phase13-shared-gpus.md): the node API /node/v1 (status, health,
    queue with cancel, priority and pause/resume per lane, runs with
    since_seq from the ledger, models, keys), opened by a node key or an
    operator on the socket. Keys as principals (key:<name>, a policy and a
    token of kind inference or node): `maluctl gateway key issue|list|
    revoke|set`. Async jobs on every face (X-Node-Mode: async or the body
    object node, 202 with a job id, /v1/jobs). The Anthropic Messages face
    (/v1/messages, non-stream and the event stream, tools, errors in
    Anthropic's shape). The node headers on every answer. The `remote`
    backend kind: a paired MaluOS GPU host reached with the pairing key the
    gateway holds in the vault (system/remote-NAME), governed by the policy
    field remote_allowed and the sensitivity gate, no forwarding chains,
    both ledgers joined by the call ids. `maluctl gateway backend add NAME
    URL --key KEY`, `maluctl gateway expose|unexpose` (the TCP listener
    applied live on reload; refuses without a key), `maluctl gateway node
    ...` and `jobs`. The sharing switch is enforced: with share off an
    inference key's call over the network is refused 503 not_shared. The
    gateway's own principal user:maluos-gateway for the pairing keys. The
    daemon reports version 0.4.0.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000

maluos-gateway (0.3.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13, shared GPUs, slice G1: the GPU sharing switch. gateway.yaml
    `share:` (enabled, contribution always|idle; unset means the chassis
    rule from maluos_gpu: a server shares, a desktop or laptop when its
    owner opts in, a laptop only while idle), `maluctl gateway share
    [status|on|off] [--when always|idle]`, and `share` in
    /v1/maluos/status (enabled, contribution, chassis, rule, configured,
    exposed). The sharing itself (the node API, `expose`) is slice G2.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:45:00 +0000

maluos-gateway (0.3.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 12 slice 9. A refused credential lookup files its grant request
    with the cause (the call's id, model, backend, class, task and time),
    so the owner's desk can say what asked.
  * Budget alerts for an agent name the agent ("agent research is at …")
    and carry its owner (maluos_agent.owner_principal_ref, read through a
    grant the component adds), so the owner's session can tell them;
    detail gains agent, owner and period.

